                                                    "countAsQuest:1":  1,
                                                    "desc:8":  "§9FOUR DYNAMOS ARE NOT ENOUGH§r\nThe output ceiling is the SUM of the dynamo row and the §9LASER SOURCE§r row - four more sockets two courses above the dynamos on the same manifold back face, same columns, exposed at every tier.\n\n  4x IV Dynamo alone       §c 32,768 EU/t§r\n  + 1 ZPM 4,096A source     536,903,680   (48.6%)\n  + 2 sources               1,073,774,592 (97.2%)\n  §2+ 3 sources               1,610,645,504 - clears a maxed tier 5§r\n\n§5§lDO §lTHIS§r\n§91.§r Fit Laser Source Hatches into the four L sockets.\n§92.§r §1PAINT§r each source, and aim its FRONT down a run of §9Laser Vacuum Pipes§r (mirrors allowed) at a §9Laser Target Hatch§r of the same colour whose own front faces back up the run.\n§93.§r The voltage tiers must match §cexactly§r.\n\n§2§lDONE §lWHEN§r\nA Laser Source Hatch and a Laser Target Hatch are in your inventory at the same time.\n§8This quest only LOOKS at what you are carrying, and it takes nothing. Hold the whole set at once, CLAIM it, and only then break the casings and set the machines into the wall. Already installed them? Wrench them back out for a moment - the check is on your inventory, not on the building.§r\n\n§5§lCHECK §lYOUR §lWORK§r\nOUTPUT stops saying CLAMPED and the laser line reads §2Lasers 4/4 fitted§r with§2 4 painted§r.\n\n[warn]A lower-tier Laser Target Hatch is DESTROYED by a higher-tier source. An unpainted source silently buffers everything it is handed and delivers nothing - which is exactly why the panel prints \"fitted\" and \"painted\" as separate numbers.[/warn]",
